{
    // One entry per server: what it is called, what it does, where
    // it points, and an icon. Everything else has a default:
    // `enabled` true, `auth_mode` dcr, `timeout` 30s. Set any of
    // them on an entry to override.
    //
    // `display_name` is what a reader sees. Derived title-casing was
    // the alternative and it produces "Rhsc", "Gworkspace" and
    // "Sumologic". Proper nouns are data, not a transformation.
    //
    // `tool_prefix` is written out rather than left to default to
    // the server key. It is what the model sees in a tool name, so a
    // renamed key should not silently rename every tool.
    //
    // `type` is the same key a VS Code mcp.json uses, so an entry
    // can move between the two unchanged.
    //
    // Nothing about a provider's OAuth is written here. Endpoints,
    // scopes, the resource identifier and the client itself are all
    // discovered at connect time from the server's own metadata.
    //
    // ── Commented-out servers ──────────────────────────────────
    // Everything below the active list is commented out because it
    // is not connected, each with the reason measured against the
    // live endpoint. They are kept rather than deleted: the URL and
    // the diagnosis are the expensive part, and re-deriving them
    // costs an afternoon. Uncomment one when its blocker is cleared.
    "mcpServers": {
        "atlan": {
            "type": "http",
            "display_name": "Atlan",
            "url": "https://mcp.atlan.com/mcp",
